# Form Handling Rules

## Form Component Structure
- Use React Hook Form for form state management.
- Integrate Zod schemas for validation.
- Use Shadcn form components for consistent UI.
- Implement proper error handling and feedback.
- Create reusable form components for common patterns.

## Form Component Pattern
```tsx
// components/forms/entity-form.tsx
'use client';

import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import { useCreateEntity } from '@/hooks/entity/use-entity-mutations';
import { 
  entitySchema, 
  type CreateEntityDto 
} from '@/types/entity';
import { 
  Form, 
  FormControl, 
  FormField, 
  FormItem, 
  FormLabel, 
  FormMessage 
} from '@/components/ui/form';
import { Input } from '@/components/ui/input';
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { toast } from 'sonner';

interface EntityFormProps {
  onSuccess?: () => void;
  defaultValues?: Partial<CreateEntityDto>;
}

export function EntityForm({ onSuccess, defaultValues }: EntityFormProps) {
  const { mutate, isPending } = useCreateEntity();
  
  const form = useForm<CreateEntityDto>({
    resolver: zodResolver(entitySchema),
    defaultValues: defaultValues || {
      name: '',
      code: '',
      description: '',
      isActive: true,
    },
  });
  
  const onSubmit = (data: CreateEntityDto) => {
    mutate(data, {
      onSuccess: () => {
        form.reset();
        onSuccess?.();
      },
      onError: (error) => {
        toast.error(`Failed to create entity: ${error.message}`);
      },
    });
  };
  
  return (
    <Form {...form}>
      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className="space-y-6">
        <FormField
          control={form.control}
          name="name"
          render={({ field }) => (
            <FormItem>
              <FormLabel>Name</FormLabel>
              <FormControl>
                <Input placeholder="Enter name" {...field} />
              </FormControl>
              <FormMessage />
            </FormItem>
          )}
        />
        
        <FormField
          control={form.control}
          name="code"
          render={({ field }) => (
            <FormItem>
              <FormLabel>Code</FormLabel>
              <FormControl>
                <Input placeholder="Enter code" {...field} />
              </FormControl>
              <FormMessage />
            </FormItem>
          )}
        />
        
        {/* Other form fields */}
        
        <Button type="submit" disabled={isPending}>
          {isPending ? 'Saving...' : 'Save'}
        </Button>
      </form>
    </Form>
  );
}
```

## Form Validation
- Use Zod schemas for form validation.
- Implement client-side validation before submission.
- Display validation errors inline next to form fields.
- Use proper error messages that are user-friendly.
- Handle server-side validation errors appropriately.

## Form Submission
- Connect forms to React Query mutations.
- Implement proper loading states during submission.
- Handle success and error cases consistently.
- Provide clear feedback to users after submission.
- Reset form state appropriately after submission.

## Complex Form Patterns
- Use form arrays for dynamic form fields.
- Implement multi-step forms with proper state management.
- Create reusable form field components.
- Handle conditional form logic appropriately.
- Implement proper form section organization.

## Form Field Components
- Create consistent form field components.
- Implement proper accessibility attributes.
- Use consistent styling across form fields.
- Implement proper form control behavior.
- Provide clear validation feedback.

## Form Performance
- Optimize form re-renders with proper field registration.
- Use controlled components only when necessary.
- Implement proper form reset behavior.
- Optimize validation performance for complex forms.
- Use proper memoization for form components.

## Server Actions Integration (Next.js 15)
- Use React 19's new Actions API for form submissions when appropriate.
- Leverage Next.js 15's server actions for server-side form handling.
- Implement proper error handling for server actions.
- Use optimistic updates for improved UX.
- Implement proper form validation with server actions.

## Form State Management
```tsx
// Example of complex form state management
import { useFieldArray } from 'react-hook-form';

// Within your form component
const { fields, append, remove } = useFieldArray({
  control: form.control,
  name: "items",
});

// Rendering dynamic fields
{fields.map((field, index) => (
  <div key={field.id} className="flex gap-4">
    <FormField
      control={form.control}
      name={`items.${index}.name`}
      render={({ field }) => (
        <FormItem className="flex-1">
          <FormLabel>Item Name</FormLabel>
          <FormControl>
            <Input {...field} />
          </FormControl>
          <FormMessage />
        </FormItem>
      )}
    />
    <Button 
      type="button" 
      variant="destructive" 
      onClick={() => remove(index)}
    >
      Remove
    </Button>
  </div>
))}

<Button
  type="button"
  variant="outline"
  onClick={() => append({ name: '', quantity: 1 })}
>
  Add Item
</Button>
```